---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { SITE } from '../../lib/site';
const lang = 'en' as const;
const toc = [
  { id: 'requirements', label: 'Requirements' },
  { id: 'connect', label: 'Connect agent' },
  { id: 'cli', label: 'Optional CLI' },
  { id: 'ghidra', label: 'Ghidra (BYO)' },
  { id: 'first', label: 'First question' },
  { id: 'links', label: 'Upstream links' },
];
---
<BaseLayout
  lang={lang}
  title="Install REA (rea-agents) — community guide | rea.run"
  description="Install REA with npx rea-agents setup, MCP registration, and bring-your-own Ghidra. Community paraphrase of upstream; verify on GitHub."
  path="/docs/install/"
>
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-6xl px-4 py-12">
    <div class="docs-layout">
      <aside class="docs-toc hidden md:block">
        <p class="section-kicker mb-3">On this page</p>
        {toc.map((item) => <a href={`#${item.id}`}>{item.label}</a>)}
      </aside>

      <article class="prose-page">
        <p class="badge">Docs · Install</p>
        <h1 class="mt-4 text-3xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-[var(--color-ink)] sm:text-4xl">Install REA</h1>
        <p class="mt-4 max-w-2xl text-base leading-7 text-[var(--color-muted)]">
          Community paraphrase of upstream install notes. Product behavior is defined by
          <a href={SITE.upstreamRepo}>github.com/morluto/rea</a>
          and the <code>rea-agents</code> package on npm. Versions change — re-check before you automate.
        </p>

        <div class="callout">
          <strong>Authorized use only.</strong> Install and run REA against software you have the right to analyze. No crack or DRM bypass guidance here.
        </div>

        <h2 id="requirements">Requirements</h2>
        <div class="mt-4 grid gap-3 sm:grid-cols-3">
          <div class="step-card"><span class="step-num">1</span><div><strong class="text-[var(--color-ink)]">Node</strong><p class="mt-1 !text-sm">22 (22.19+), 24 (24.11+), or 26+ plus npm (per upstream).</p></div></div>
          <div class="step-card"><span class="step-num">2</span><div><strong class="text-[var(--color-ink)]">MCP client</strong><p class="mt-1 !text-sm">Claude Code, Codex, Cursor, Gemini CLI, Windsurf, Grok Build, or other MCP clients — or CLI alone.</p></div></div>
          <div class="step-card"><span class="step-num">3</span><div><strong class="text-[var(--color-ink)]">Native engines</strong><p class="mt-1 !text-sm">Deep native analysis needs existing Hopper, Ghidra, or IDA. Static JS/Electron does not.</p></div></div>
        </div>

        <h2 id="connect">Connect your coding agent</h2>
        <p>Ask your agent to run setup with approval, or run it yourself:</p>
        <pre><code>npx rea-agents@latest setup</code></pre>
        <p>
          Choose your client, review the plan, and approve changes. Setup registers the MCP server and matching investigation skill, backing up existing config. <strong>Restart the client</strong> afterward.
        </p>
        <p>Manual MCP registration shape (confirm against upstream if your client needs hand-edited JSON):</p>
        <pre><code>{`{
  "mcpServers": {
    "rea": {
      "command": "npx",
      "args": ["-y", "rea-agents@latest", "mcp"]
    }
  }
}`}</code></pre>
        <p>Pin an exact <code>rea-agents@VERSION</code> when you need reproducible installs.</p>

        <h2 id="cli">Optional: global CLI</h2>
        <pre><code>npm install --global rea-agents</code></pre>

        <h2 id="ghidra">Ghidra (bring your own)</h2>
        <p>REA does not install Ghidra or Java. Export absolute paths, then doctor + setup:</p>
        <pre><code>{`export GHIDRA_INSTALL_DIR=/absolute/path/to/ghidra_PUBLIC
export JAVA_HOME=/absolute/path/to/jdk-21
npx -y rea-agents@latest doctor --provider ghidra --json
npx rea-agents@latest setup`}</code></pre>
        <p>
          Supported host / Ghidra / JDK combinations are defined upstream — see
          <a href="https://github.com/morluto/rea/blob/main/docs/installation.md">docs/installation.md</a> in the GitHub repo.
        </p>

        <h2 id="first">First question to try</h2>
        <p>After reconnecting the agent, give an <strong>absolute path</strong> to a target you may analyze and a specific question (entry points, export paths, a named feature). Prefer Evidence + unknowns over speculative narratives.</p>

        <h2 id="links">Upstream links</h2>
        <ul>
          <li><a href={SITE.upstreamRepo}>GitHub: morluto/rea</a></li>
          <li><a href={SITE.upstreamNpm}>npm: rea-agents</a></li>
          <li><a href="/blog/ghidra-mcp-with-rea/">Community: Ghidra MCP with REA</a></li>
          <li><a href="/compliance/">Compliance</a></li>
        </ul>
      </article>
    </div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
